adr: 0300
file: selfhost/apfront.pas
kills: protected_hint
why: ADR-0283's warning judged a parameter where 6.7.3.1's word belongs to the section, so `var written, read_: integer` with one name written through was advised to take `protected` -- advice that does not compile, since the word would protect `written` too. Judging the section by the last of its names restores exactly that: `Mixed` in tests/dialect/protected_hint.pas is warned about again and its .warn sidecar says nothing of it.
--- old
      whole := true;
      r := q;
      while (r <> nil) and (r^.sym^.paramSection = sec) do begin
        if not ProtectableCandidate(r^.sym) then whole := false;
        r := r^.next
      end;
--- new
      whole := true;
      r := q;
      while (r <> nil) and (r^.sym^.paramSection = sec) do begin
        whole := ProtectableCandidate(r^.sym);
        r := r^.next
      end;
